  "arithmetic": {
    "question": "does the medium require anything the organism cannot see now",
    "oracle_bound": "`oracle` moves toward the globally richest cell every step. It knows more than any memory can (memory knows only what it has seen), so its reward bounds from above what memory could be worth.",
    "p_need": "ceil(ln(M/(M-m)) / -ln(1-r)), the return period that lets a cell regrow",
    "why_income_is_m": "with income = m the organism takes exactly its upkeep, so the only remaining question is whether the cell has regrown on return",
    "prediction": "if both neighbours are visible (read_budget = 3) the richest cell is always one step away and therefore already seen: oracle, sighted and intact should coincide exactly. With read_budget <= 1 the medium becomes partially observable and the oracle should beat every memoryless arm - the question is then whether our memory can exploit it",
    "grid": "read_budget in {0,1,2,3} x P_need in {1,2}"
  },
