  "limitations": [
    "the oracle knows the globally richest cell. That is more than memory can know, so it bounds memory from above; it is not an achievable policy.",
    "`income = m` and `move_cost = 0` by construction: with a non-zero move cost the return period shifts and `P_need` stops being a property of the medium alone.",
    "the probe wraps movement around a ring. `Field` and `Life` do not wrap, and without wrapping a one-dimensional walk cannot have a return period longer than two, so `P_need >= 3` is unreachable by construction.",
    "one organism, uniform ring, no competition and no sharing: this bounds the value of information, not a population's fate.",
    "arms that share a dynamics hash are declared as one arm, and there are many: with a uniform ring almost every policy that keeps moving produces the same trajectory. That is the finding, not a bug in the declarations - but it also means this grid cannot separate policies that differ only in which rich cell they choose.",
    "memory here stores the cell the organism stands on. If the medium becomes partially observable only for cells it has never stood on, this implementation cannot exploit it even when the oracle shows the information is worth having."
